    "verdict": "true-positive",
    "reasoning": "Verified end-to-end. `bunRoutes[`${assetPrefix}/island/:componentName`]` (Mochi.ts:1559) calls `buildRequestContext(req, server, { kind: 'island' })`, and `KIND_POLICY.island` in runtime/requestSetup.ts:67 is `{ timeout: false, trailingSlash: false, csrf: false, debugBar: false }`. `middleware` is invoked at exactly three sites in Mochi.ts — 991 (page), 1240 (api), 1922 (composedFetch/assets) — and nowhere in the island handler; `resolveLimiter`/`checkRouteLimit` likewise only run in the `isMochiPage`/`isMochiApi` branches, so the endpoint has no rate limit either. Only the `protection` PoW gate (cfg.protection, requestSetup.ts:130) and the `serverIslandPaths` membership check apply. Lines 1574-1586 confirm `if (signedProps) {decrypt} else {decodedProps = {}}` — an absent token is treated as 'no props', not as a missing capability, so `GET /_mochi/island/<key>` renders the island with `props={}`, empty `locals`, and no authz. The docs make this a genuine trap: types.ts:528 says `handle` wraps 'every incoming request — authentication, logging, headers'; docs/120-middleware.md's `event.kind` table lists only page/api/asset/fallback/error and documents only WS/SSE as middleware-exempt; and docs/70-server-islands.md:222 actively tells authors to 'fetch data inside the island' via `getRequestContext()` rather than through props — exactly the shape that leaks when the render runs unauthenticated. One correction to the finding: the claim that prop-less islands routinely hit this branch is wrong. svelteAstPreprocess.ts:295-318 always injects `islandId: __mochi_iid` into the envelope, so every emitted `<mochi-server-island>` carries a `signed-props` attribute ('Server islands always emit signed-props') — the empty-props branch is reachable only by a hand-crafted request. That does not weaken the vulnerability (the server still does not require the token), only the 'mainstream path' framing. Discoverability is a real but surmountable obstacle: the key is `<localName>_<base36 Bun.hash(project-relative path)>` (islandIdentity, line 492), an unkeyed deterministic hash the code comment confirms is stable across machines, so it is computable offline from a guessed source path and visible in the HTML of any page that uses the island. Keeping HIGH: conditional on app shape (authz in `handle` + a defer island that doesn't read `locals`), but a real confused-deputy with no framework-side mitigation and no documentation of the exemption."
