    "adjustedSeverity": "BUG",
    "reasoning": "The contract mismatch is real. docs/147-events.md:110 documents the `request` event's `path` as 'URL pathname', and extensions.ts:41 says 'For requests this is the URL path', while every emission site passes `url.pathname + url.search` — Mochi.ts:1002 (page), 1250 (api), 1276 (ws reject), 1454 (file), 1715 (image), 1927 (asset/fallback), 522 (emitError), and requestSetup.ts:101 for early exits. dev/consoleLogger.ts:76-83 forwards `payload.path` into `emit`, which prints it verbatim (line 541), and the docs' own subscriber example at 147-events.md:50-51 passes `path` as a third-party metrics tag. The secondary bug is also real: `silenceInternalRoutes` compares `path === '/.well-known/appspecific/com.chrome.devtools.json'` (consoleLogger.ts:432), an exact match that now fails whenever a query string is present (the sibling checks use `startsWith` and still work). Two corrections. The finding over-attributes the doc error: 147-events.md:311/331/341 document `error`, `action:invoke` and `action:complete` as 'URL pathname + search', i.e. correctly, and `MochiRequestEvent.path` carries no JSDoc at all in events.ts — only the `request` table is wrong. And at the production default `level: 'warn'`, only 5xx/slow lines print (emit escalates on `status >= 500 || duration >= slow`), so routine URLs are not written out by default. Downgrading to BUG: logging the full request target is conventional practice, so the defect here is the typed/documented contract diverging from the implementation (plus the broken exact-match filter), not a novel secret-exposure channel."
